  "notes": "Term-by-term sequence transcribed verbatim from the official 2024-2025 American International College 'Program Plan' for Biology (School of Business, Arts and Sciences). Semester totals printed on the plan: 14+17+14+14+14+17+14+16 = 120 credits (TOTAL CREDITS: 120). The program is a Bachelor of Science (Four-Year BS Program) per the official aic.edu program page. MAT1840 College Algebra and Trigonometry is 4 credits; MAT2400 Calculus I is 4 credits; MAT2004 Biostatistics is 3 credits (Gen Ed Category 1). Lab courses are 4 credits and include the lab section (e.g., BIO1400 lecture + BIO1401 lab = 4 credits total; PHY1600 + PHY1601 = 4 credits). The 'BIO3XXX, Biology elective, with lab' slots are recorded as 4-credit biology electives (majors must complete a minimum of 8 elective credits in biology at or above the 3000 level; CHE3200 with lab may count). Senior-year research/internship slots: students choose BIO4833 Research Problems or BIO4899 Biology Internship (or an elective for the Senior Fall slot). The plan notes MAT1630 College Algebra is recommended for students needing math support, pushing MAT1840/MAT2400 to Year 2 (MAT1630 counts as a general elective). General Education categories per the 2024-2025 plan: Cat 1 Scientific World (math + science with lab), Cat 2 Self and Others, Cat 3 Interdisciplinarity (ENG1202 + INT courses), Cat 4 Arts and Humanities, Cat 5 Professional Readiness (AIC1005/AIC1100 + AIC3005). tccns mirrors the local course code (AIC is in Massachusetts; no TCCNS). transfer_confidence is 'core_only'.",
